# Ship and verify without blocking

When the user asks to push, deploy, and/or verify on production (or similar end-to-end ship requests):

- Do not stop for non-essential confirmations or questionnaires.
- Prefer action: run tests → commit → push → open/merge MR when credentials allow → wait for deploy → verify production → report results.
- Only ask when a hard blocker exists (missing secrets you cannot obtain, destructive irreversible action needing explicit consent, or genuine ambiguity that changes product behavior).
- Keep the final report concise: what shipped, what was verified, any remaining backend/index limitations.
